_line_start":392},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n 21.1.24\n2\n and came fully into effect on 1.6.24","tree_line_end":414,"tree_line_start":404},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n 29.9.21\n3\n and was provisionally applied from 01.11.21. It came fully in effect from 1.10.23","tree_line_end":425,"tree_line_start":415},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n 11.10.23\n4\n and came into effect on 1.1.24.","tree_line_end":436,"tree_line_start":426},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n \nSS (Ireland) Order 2019\n; 2\n \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024\n3 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n; 4\n \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023  \n   ","tree_line_end":468,"tree_line_start":437},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. The TCA\n1 \nprovisionally applied from 1.1.21 and came fully into effect on 1.5.21.\n ","tree_line_end":477,"tree_line_start":469},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nTCA","tree_line_end":487,"tree_line_start":478},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Background","tree_line_end":492,"tree_line_start":488},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n \n From 1.1.21, individuals and their family members moving between the UK, Ireland, Gibraltar, \nSwitzerland, Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway, who are not covered by the","tree_line_end":499,"tree_line_start":493},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n \n \n EU-UK-WA \nor","tree_line_end":518,"tree_line_start":500},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2.\n \n \n \nUK-EEA EFTA Separation Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":538,"tree_line_start":519},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 3.\n \n \n UK-Swiss Citizens’ Rights Agreement\n \n \n \ncan no longer rely on protections under EU law for social security co-ordination.","tree_line_end":558,"tree_line_start":539},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5. The UK has made reciprocal arrangements with","tree_line_end":562,"tree_line_start":559},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n Ireland\n1","tree_line_end":572,"tree_line_start":563},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n Gibraltar\n2","tree_line_end":581,"tree_line_start":573},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n \n Switzerland\n3","tree_line_end":592,"tree_line_start":582},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway\n4","tree_line_end":602,"tree_line_start":593},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"which gives effect to social security co-ordination between the UK and those countries from the dates \nas shown at paragraph 2 of this memo.","tree_line_end":607,"tree_line_start":603},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n \nSS (Ireland) Order 2019\n; 2\n \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024\n3 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n; 4\n \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023  \n   ","tree_line_end":639,"tree_line_start":608},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":643,"tree_line_start":640},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6.\n \n The Trade & Co-operation Agreement1 [TCA] social security protocol provides for social security co-\nordination between EU Member States and the UK from the end of the transition period on 31.12.20 and \napplied from 1.1.21 for those not in scope of the EU-UK-WA.\n ","tree_line_end":652,"tree_line_start":644},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\nTCA","tree_line_end":662,"tree_line_start":653},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Ireland","tree_line_end":667,"tree_line_start":663},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7. The Schedule to the 2019 Order\n1\n broadly replicates existing legislation\n2\n ensuring that there is no \nchange in the social security rights of British nationals, Irish nationals and their family members moving \nbetween the UK and Ireland as a result of the UK’s withdrawal from the EU.\n \n ","tree_line_end":683,"tree_line_start":668},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 2019\n; 2 \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004 ","tree_line_end":699,"tree_line_start":684},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8.\n \n When making a claim for long-term care benefits from the UK, persons moving from","tree_line_end":705,"tree_line_start":700},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \nthe UK to Ireland are able to benefit from the broader legal test of whether they can show a \n‘genuine and sufficient link’ to the UK \nor","tree_line_end":717,"tree_line_start":706},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n Ireland to the UK, the narrower ‘past-presence’ legal test is applied (see Note).","tree_line_end":724,"tree_line_start":718},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n Periods of insurance in Ireland will be applied to said persons’ when the PPT is applied to them. For \nfull guidance on the PPT see \nDMG Chapter 07\n.","tree_line_end":736,"tree_line_start":725},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"9. When a person in receipt of a pension from both the UK and Ireland makes a claim for","tree_line_end":740,"tree_line_start":737},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nsickness benefit \nor","tree_line_end":749,"tree_line_start":741},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2\n. maternity and paternity benefits \nor","tree_line_end":758,"tree_line_start":750},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n long term care benefits\nthe competent state for the payment of the benefit is the state the person has been subject to the\n  \nlegislation the longest.","tree_line_end":768,"tree_line_start":759},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10. The social security rights of UK and Irish nationals provided for under the Common Travel Area \nagreement are unchanged by the 2019 Order\n1\n.","tree_line_end":777,"tree_line_start":769},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 2019","tree_line_end":787,"tree_line_start":778},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Gibraltar","tree_line_end":792,"tree_line_start":788},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"11. For persons not in scope of the","tree_line_end":796,"tree_line_start":793},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \n \nEU-UK-WA \nor","tree_line_end":808,"tree_line_start":797},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n \n \nUK-EEA EFTA Separation Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":820,"tree_line_start":809},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3\n.\n \n \n \nUK-Swiss Citizens’ Rights Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":833,"tree_line_start":821},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4.\n \n \n \nUK-Swiss Social Security Convention","tree_line_end":843,"tree_line_start":834},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"the Schedule to the 2024 Order\n1\n replicates existing legislation\n2\n ensuring that there is no change to \nthe social security rights of individuals and their family members moving between the UK and \nGibraltar as a\n \n result of the UK’s withdrawal from the EU.","tree_line_end":860,"tree_line_start":844},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024;\n \n2\n \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004; \n ","tree_line_end":879,"tree_line_start":861},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"12. The 2024 Order\n1\n came into effect on 1.6.24.\n \n To ensure continuity, claims and awards made","tree_line_end":889,"tree_line_start":880},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n for periods on or before 31.12.20 will be determined under the earlier agreement\n2\n, which \nprovided that previous legislation\n3\n applied \nor","tree_line_end":908,"tree_line_start":890},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n \n \nfrom 1.1.21 will be determined under the 2024 Order\n1\n. However, Article 65 (3) does not permit \nclaims to be backdated between 1.6.24 to 1.1.21 (i.e. no award can be backdated between those \ntwo dates).","tree_line_end":924,"tree_line_start":909},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024; 2 Exchange of letters (Gibraltar) Order 1974; ","tree_line_end":934,"tree_line_start":925},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3 \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004 ","tree_line_end":944,"tree_line_start":935},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Switzerland","tree_line_end":949,"tree_line_start":945},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"13. The Schedule to the 2021 Order\n1\n has fewer or modified social security rights and applies to all \nindividuals and their family members moving between the UK and\n \n Switzerland with the following \nexceptions,\n ","tree_line_end":962,"tree_line_start":950},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n for Benefits in Kind, only Swiss, UK and EU nationals (plus stateless persons and refugees) are in \nscope for UK healthcare where the UK is competent","tree_line_end":970,"tree_line_start":963},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n only Swiss, UK and EU nationals (plus stateless persons and refugees) are in scope for Swiss \ncash benefits and healthcare where Switzerland is competent.","tree_line_end":978,"tree_line_start":971},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n See paragraph 15 for a further explanation of the changes to social security rights under the 2021 \nOrder. \n ","tree_line_end":986,"tree_line_start":979},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021","tree_line_end":996,"tree_line_start":987},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Iceland, Norway and Liechtenstein","tree_line_end":1001,"tree_line_start":997},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"14. The Schedule to the 2023\n1\n Order has fewer or modified social security rights for individuals and their \nfamily members moving between the UK, Iceland, Norway, and Liechtenstein. \n \nSee paragraph 15 for a \nfurther explanation of those changes.","tree_line_end":1013,"tree_line_start":1002},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023\n ","tree_line_end":1024,"tree_line_start":1014},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Changes","tree_line_end":1029,"tree_line_start":1025},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"15. For Switzerland, Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway, social security co-ordination under the TCA\n1\n and \nthe 2021 Order\n2\n and 2023 Order\n3 \ndiffer from the rights that exist for persons covered by the EU-UK-WA. ","tree_line_end":1046,"tree_line_start":1030},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nTCA\n; 2 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n; 3 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023","tree_line_end":1068,"tree_line_start":1047},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"16. The rules for aggregation and exportability continue to apply to State Retirement Pension.","tree_line_end":1072,"tree_line_start":1069},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"17. The rules for the exporting of \n ","tree_line_end":1077,"tree_line_start":1073},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n 1.\n WMA","tree_line_end":1087,"tree_line_start":1078},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n2.\n WPA \nand","tree_line_end":1100,"tree_line_start":1088},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n3.\n WP","tree_line_end":1111,"tree_line_start":1101},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n continue to apply.","tree_line_end":1119,"tree_line_start":1112},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"18. New claims may be made for WP for deaths occurring prior to 6.4.17.","tree_line_end":1123,"tree_line_start":1120},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"19. Exporting is not allowable for an award of","tree_line_end":1127,"tree_line_start":1124},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n1.\n AA","tree_line_end":1138,"tree_line_start":1128},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n 2.\n CA","tree_line_end":1147,"tree_line_start":1139},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n 3.\n DLA (Care)","tree_line_end":1157,"tree_line_start":1148},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n4.\n WFP (see Note 1)","tree_line_end":1168,"tree_line_start":1158},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n unless the claimant is within scope of the EU-UK-WA.\n ","tree_line_end":1177,"tree_line_start":1169},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 1:\n \n For WFP the claimant must be within the full scope of the EU-UK-WA.","tree_line_end":1184,"tree_line_start":1178},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note 2:\n \n For guidance on the differences between how social security benefits are co-ordinated under \nthe TCA and the EU-UK-WA see \nDMG memo 11/22\n and \nChapter 7, Part 2, Appendix 3 of the DMG\n.","tree_line_end":1202,"tree_line_start":1185},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Interim provisions","tree_line_end":1207,"tree_line_start":1203},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"20. From 1.1.21 for those who were not in scope of the Separation Agreements, only pensions were \ncoordinated. This means that for claimants between 1.1.21 and 31.12.23 there were less rights but this \nwas temporary pending the new agreement and only applied to those who were not covered by the \nSeparation Agreements.","tree_line_end":1214,"tree_line_start":1208},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n The Separation Agreements are shown at paragraph 5 and are listed 1-4.","tree_line_end":1220,"tree_line_start":1215},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Norway","tree_line_end":1225,"tree_line_start":1221},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"21. From the end of the transition period on 31.12.20 to the entry into force of the 2023 Order\n1\n on 1.1.24, \nthe UK and Norway applied the 1991 Agreement between them as amended by 2020 Exchange of \nLetters. These were implemented by the 2020 Order\n2\n.","tree_line_end":1239,"tree_line_start":1226},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023\n; 2 \nSS (Norway) Order 2020 No. 1597","tree_line_end":1255,"tree_line_start":1240},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Switzerland","tree_line_end":1260,"tree_line_start":1256},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"22. After the end of the transition period until the entry into force of the Agreement on 1.11.21\n1\n, the UK \nand Switzerland used the historic 1968 Convention between the two countries to coordinate social \nsecurity.","tree_line_end":1270,"tree_line_start":1261},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021","tree_line_end":1280,"tree_line_start":1271},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Annotations","tree_line_end":1285,"tree_line_start":1281},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Please annotate the following paragraphs with Memo 07-24 \n071740,   \n071753, 071754  \n, \n071761\n, \n071779\n, \n071785\n, \n071790\n, \n071795\n, \n071801\n, \n071805\n, \n071912\n.","tree_line_e